{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-euclidean-norm-comparison-flat","title":"lem:riemannian-euclidean-norm-comparison-flat","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2340,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:riemannian-euclidean-norm-comparison-flat","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:norm-comparison-compact-core]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-energy-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:euclidean-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:riemannian-euclidean-norm-comparison-flat","line":3796,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Norm Comparison on $\\mathbb{R}^n$]\n\\label{lem:riemannian-euclidean-norm-comparison-flat}\n\n\\uses{lem:norm-comparison-compact-core, lem:metric-energy-smooth, def:riemannian-metric, ex:euclidean-metric}\n\n\n\n\nLet $g$ be Riemannian on $\\mathbb R^n$ and $\\widetilde g$ Euclidean. For every compact $K\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$, some $c,C>0$ satisfy\n\\[\nc|v|_{\\widetilde g}\\le|v|_g\\le C|v|_{\\widetilde g},\n\\qquad x\\in K, v\\in T_x\\mathbb R^n.\n\\]\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:norm-comparison-compact-core, lem:metric-energy-smooth, ex:euclidean-metric}\n\\sketch Under $T\\mathbb R^n\\cong\\mathbb R^n\\times\\mathbb R^n$, Lemma \\ref{lem:metric-energy-smooth} gives continuity of $(x,v)\\mapsto g_x(v,v)$, and positivity is that of $g$. Apply Lemma \\ref{lem:norm-comparison-compact-core} to $q_x=g_x$ and use $|v|_{\\widetilde g}=|v|$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Norm Comparison on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathbb {R}^n$\">$\\mathbb {R}^n$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d6575636c696465616e2d6e6f726d2d636f6d70617269736f6e2d666c6174\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anorm-comparison-compact-core\">↗ lem:norm-comparison-compact-core</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ametric-energy-smooth\">↗ lem:metric-energy-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23ex%3Aeuclidean-metric\">↗ ex:euclidean-metric</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> be Riemannian on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathbb R^n$\">$\\mathbb R^n$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\widetilde g$\">$\\widetilde g$</span> Euclidean. For every compact <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K\\subseteq \\mathbb R^n$\">$K\\subseteq \\mathbb R^n$</span>, some <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c,C&gt;0$\">$c,C&gt;0$</span> satisfy <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  c|v|_{\\widetilde g}\\le |v|_g\\le C|v|_{\\widetilde g}, \\qquad x\\in K, v\\in T_x\\mathbb R^n.  \\]\">\\[  c|v|_{\\widetilde g}\\le |v|_g\\le C|v|_{\\widetilde g}, \\qquad x\\in K, v\\in T_x\\mathbb R^n.  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anorm-comparison-compact-core\">↗ lem:norm-comparison-compact-core</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ametric-energy-smooth\">↗ lem:metric-energy-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23ex%3Aeuclidean-metric\">↗ ex:euclidean-metric</a> \\sketch Under <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T\\mathbb R^n\\cong \\mathbb R^n\\times \\mathbb R^n$\">$T\\mathbb R^n\\cong \\mathbb R^n\\times \\mathbb R^n$</span>, Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ametric-energy-smooth\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-energy-smooth\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6d65747269632d656e657267792d736d6f6f7468\">15</a> gives continuity of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(x,v)\\mapsto g_x(v,v)$\">$(x,v)\\mapsto g_x(v,v)$</span>, and positivity is that of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span>. Apply Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anorm-comparison-compact-core\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:norm-comparison-compact-core\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6e6f726d2d636f6d70617269736f6e2d636f6d706163742d636f7265\">15</a> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_x=g_x$\">$q_x=g_x$</span> and use <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|v|_{\\widetilde g}=|v|$\">$|v|_{\\widetilde g}=|v|$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:norm-comparison-compact-core","next":"references/LeeRiemanni