ivity is that of $g$. Apply Lemma \\ref{lem:norm-comparison-compact-core} to $q_x=g_x$ and use $|v|_{\\widetilde g}=|v|$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:norm-comparison-compact-core","title":"lem:norm-comparison-compact-core","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-energy-smooth","title":"lem:metric-energy-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:euclidean-metric","title":"ex:euclidean-metric","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}